Z||000000||Alex2004||12-28-2000||10:09 PM||||how do you change the dash pocket thing without taking out the dash? Or can you? I have the pocket out of an 86 GT that we bought from a junk yard, and we basicaly striped it of all it's good parts. The dash had cracks around the edge so i didn't use it but i took the pocket out of it. I have an 84 se with the ugly plain pocket. Is there anyway i can change it w/o taking the dash out????? Thanks... <BR>Alex...<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||12-28-2000||10:58 PM||||  Alex, there is no way to change the dash pocket without removing the dash. Removing the dash however, is fairly easy. You have to remove the entire gauge pod and the center radio pod console (black vinyl) and the metal bracke the the pod screws to. It's not as daunting as it sounds. It should take about 30 mins to remove the dash. Once the dash is out you have to remove 6 7mm screws that hold the duct on,, then you can remove the pocket. The pocket is held on by four self threading speednuts. It's that simple. E-Mail me if you need any more help. bartlettds@lvcm.com<P><BR> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||6
